      "topic": "Nouns",
      "difficulty": "Hard",
      "q": "[Nouns Advanced #3] In sentence correction, identify the option that rectifies the misplaced modifier:\n'Having compiled the performance metrics, the quarterly report was submitted by the team lead.'",
      "o": [
        "Having compiled the performance metrics, the team lead submitted the quarterly report.",
        "Compiled with performance metrics, the quarterly report was submitted by the team lead.",
        "The quarterly report having been compiled with metrics submitted the team lead.",
        "Having compiled performance metrics was submitted in the quarterly report by the lead."
      ],
      "a": 0,
      "h": "Who compiled the performance metrics? The modifier must directly precede that person.",
      "e": "In the original sentence, 'Having compiled the performance metrics' incorrectly modifies 'the quarterly report' (a report cannot compile metrics). The modifier must immediately precede 'the team lead', who actually performed the compiling.",
      "step": "Step 1: Identify participial phrase: 'Having compiled...'.\nStep 2: Identify semantic agent: 'the team lead'.\nStep 3: Agent must follow the comma immediately to prevent a dangling modifier.",
      "tech": "Participial modifier alignment.",
      "formula": "",
      "code": ""
