      "difficulty": "Hard",
      "q": "[Pronouns Critical #5] Read the following argument and identify the fundamental logical flaw:\n'Every employee who received the bonus exceeded their quarterly target. Therefore, any employee who exceeds their quarterly target will inevitably receive the bonus.'",
      "o": [
        "Affirming the consequent (confusing a necessary condition with a sufficient condition)",
        "Ad hominem attack against non-bonus recipients",
        "False dilemma assuming only two quarterly outcomes exist",
        "Circular reasoning assuming the conclusion in the premise"
      ],
      "a": 0,
      "h": "P implies Q does not mean Q implies P.",
      "e": "The argument states: 'Bonus implies Exceeded Target' (P -> Q). It concludes: 'Exceeded Target implies Bonus' (Q -> P). This is the classic formal fallacy of affirming the consequent (the converse error).",
      "step": "Step 1: Formalize premise: Bonus -> Exceeded Target.\nStep 2: Formalize conclusion: Exceeded Target -> Bonus.\nStep 3: Invalid inversion of conditional statement (Affirming the Consequent).",
      "tech": "Formal propositional logic validation.",
      "formula": "(P \\implies Q) \\not\\implies (Q \\implies P)",
