      "q": "[Degrees of Comparison Advanced #2] Select the word that accurately completes the philosophical distinction:\n'While the researcher's methodology appeared sound on the surface, peer review revealed it to be wholly ______, lacking any reproducible empirical grounding.'",
      "o": [
        "specious",
        "scrupulous",
        "salubrious",
        "sagacious"
      ],
      "a": 0,
      "h": "'Specious' means superficially plausible, but actually wrong.",
      "e": "'Specious' describes an argument or methodology that seems right or attractive at first glance, but is actually deceptive and flawed upon closer inspection. 'Scrupulous' means diligent; 'salubrious' means health-giving; 'sagacious' means wise.",
      "step": "Step 1: Context clue: 'appeared sound on the surface' contrasted with 'lacking reproducible grounding'.\nStep 2: Contrast requires a word meaning superficially plausible but false.\nStep 3: 'Specious' is the precise contextual match.",
      "tech": "Contextual semantic contrast.",
      "formula": "",
