      "topic": "Word Usage",
      "difficulty": "Hard",
      "q": "[Word Usage Critical #5] Read the following argument and identify the fundamental logical flaw:\n'Every employee who received the bonus exceeded their quarterly target. Therefore, any employee who exceeds their quarterly target will inevitably receive the bonus.'",
      "o": [
        "Affirming the consequent (confusing a necessary condition with a sufficient condition)",
        "Ad hominem attack against non-bonus recipients",
        "False dilemma assuming only two quarterly outcomes exist",
        "Circular reasoning assuming the conclusion in the premise"
      ],
      "a": 0,
      "h": "P implies Q does not mean Q implies P.",
