      "q": "[Blood Relations Cubes #2] A cube painted red on all six faces is sliced into 125 identical smaller cubes using parallel cuts. How many smaller cubes have exactly two red faces painted?",
      "o": [
        "36",
        "48",
        "54",
        "24"
      ],
      "a": 0,
      "h": "Cubes with exactly two painted faces lie along the edges, excluding the 8 corners.",
      "e": "For a cube divided into n^3 = 125 cubes, n = 5. A cube has 12 edges. The cubes with exactly 2 faces painted lie along the interior of the edges: Formula = 12 * (n - 2). With n = 5: 12 * (5 - 2) = 12 * 3 = 36 cubes.",
      "step": "Step 1: n^3 = 125 => n = 5.\nStep 2: Cubes with 2 painted faces lie on edges between corners.\nStep 3: Cubes per edge = n - 2 = 5 - 2 = 3.\nStep 4: Total edges = 12.\nStep 5: Total = 12 * 3 = 36.",
      "tech": "Spatial solid geometry decomposition formula.",
      "formula": "N_{\\text{2-faces}} = 12(n - 2)",
