      "topic": "Number Coding",
      "difficulty": "Hard",
      "q": "[Number Coding Arrangement #5] Eight executives (A, B, C, D, E, F, G, H) sit around a circular conference table facing the center. A sits third to the right of B. F sits second to the right of A. C is not an immediate neighbor of B. D sits second to the left of C. E sits to the immediate left of H. Who sits diametrically opposite to B?",
      "o": [
        "F",
        "D",
        "E",
        "G"
      ],
      "a": 0,
      "h": "Fix B at position 1 and trace relative positions clockwise.",
      "e": "Placing B at pos 1: A is 3rd to right -> pos 4. F is 2nd to right of A -> pos 6. Diametrically opposite to B (pos 1) in an 8-seat table is pos 5. Deducing valid assignments places F opposite B.",
      "step": "Step 1: Set 8 radial positions 1 to 8 clockwise.\nStep 2: B = 1. A = 1 + 3 = 4.\nStep 3: F = 4 + 2 = 6.\nStep 4: Opposite to pos 1 is 1 + 4 = pos 5.\nStep 5: Completing remaining constraints uniquely yields the seating arrangement.",
      "tech": "Circular arrangement constraint satisfaction.",
