      "e": "In classical syllogistic logic, the middle term 'superconductors' is predicate of an affirmative universal premise (undistributed) and subject of a particular premise (undistributed). An undistributed middle term creates a fallacy, meaning no valid relationship can be inferred between 'quantum processors' and 'high-frequency oscillators'.",
      "step": "Step 1: Premise 1 (A-type): All Q are S (S is undistributed).\nStep 2: Premise 2 (I-type): Some S are H (both S and H undistributed).\nStep 3: Middle term S is not distributed in either premise.\nStep 4: Fallacy of the Undistributed Middle -> No valid conclusion.",
