      "id": "logical_paper_fold_h_003",
      "category": "Verbal Ability and Logical Reasoning",
      "group": "Logical Reasoning",
      "topic_id": "logical_paper_fold",
      "topic": "Paper Folding",
      "difficulty": "Hard",
      "q": "[Paper Folding Sets #3] In a group of 50 researchers, 30 are proficient in Python, 25 are proficient in C++, and 10 are proficient in neither. How many researchers are proficient in BOTH Python and C++?",
      "o": [
        "15",
        "10",
        "20",
        "25"
      ],
      "a": 0,
      "h": "Total proficient in at least one = Total - Neither. Then use Principle of Inclusion-Exclusion.",
      "e": "Total researchers = 50. Neither = 10, so Proficient in at least one = 50 - 10 = 40. By Inclusion-Exclusion: n(P \u222a C) = n(P) + n(C) - n(P \u2229 C) => 40 = 30 + 25 - n(P \u2229 C) => 40 = 55 - n(P \u2229 C) => n(P \u2229 C) = 15.",
      "step": "Step 1: n(Universal) = 50.\nStep 2: n(P \u222a C) = 50 - 10 = 40.\nStep 3: n(P \u222a C) = n(P) + n(C) - n(P \u2229 C).\nStep 4: 40 = 30 + 25 - Intersection => Intersection = 55 - 40 = 15.",
      "tech": "Principle of Inclusion-Exclusion.",
      "formula": "n(A \\cap B) = n(A) + n(B) - n(A \\cup B)",
      "code": ""
